+# Route A Gate 3 evidence design (cave strategy) — 2026-10-22
+
+**Owner:** Member 4 (verification), after the ownership handoff in
+`docs_BinaryRepair/handoffs/13-route-a-ownership-handoff.md`.
+**Scope:** complete the Route A design and make the Gate 3 evidence package
+producible; **every test and every binary-touching command runs in the
+disposable guest**, never on the Windows host (`AGENTS.md`).
+**Status:** design + code + tests written; **tests not executed on the host**.
+Gate 3 remains `CONDITIONALLY FEASIBLE` until the guest run and an independent
+replay exist. Gate 4 is out of scope here.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Accepted repair design (unchanged behaviour)
+
+Strategy C, cave call redirect:
+
+| Item | Value |
+|---|---|
+| patch site | `0x401304`, 5-byte `call strcpy@plt` (`e8 c7 fd ff ff`) |
+| redirect | `call` cave at `0x4018e9` (`e8 e0 05 00 00`), displaces the call as a unit |
+| valid path | cave tail-jumps to `strcpy@plt` and returns to **`0x401309`** |
+| invalid path | `fprintf(stderr, msg)` then `exit_group(1)`, never returns to `main` |
+| added code | 72 bytes at `0x4018e9` (inline NUL scan, bound `max_valid_input_bytes`) |
+| added data | 42-byte exact stderr immediately after the code (RIP-relative only) |
+| header change | extend the existing R-X `PT_LOAD` `p_filesz`/`p_memsz` `0x8e9` -> `0x1000` |
+| new segments/imports/relocations | none; `fprintf@0x401120` and `stderr@0x404080` already exist |
+
+The candidate is reproducible: the same original + plan must produce byte-identical
+output, whose recorded SHA-256 is
+`f3cb9cbb503fb0d47ebebab7053fa2ed37b7876ffe5122157d31fefc783f9fa7`.
+
+**Correction to earlier text:** the instruction after the 5-byte call is `0x401309`,
+not `0x401308`. Handoff 09 §4.1 entry 1 is corrected; any gdb breakpoint on
+`0x401308` is mid-instruction and must be changed to `0x401309`.
+
+---
+
+## 2. What this design adds over the probe
+
+The 2026-10-22 probe proved the repair works on a GitHub Actions runner. It did
+**not** produce Gate 3 evidence (network during install, not the team guest, no
+isolation). This design closes the static half and defines the runtime half.
+
+1. **Complete edit manifest (schema 2)** — `edit-manifest.json` now lists the
+   displaced 5 original bytes, the exact 114 added bytes with file offsets and
+   hashes, the two changed header fields with before/after values and file
+   offsets, every changed file interval, the intended interval set, the writer,
+   the termination mechanism, and the tool versions.
+2. **Extended static audit** — program-header invariants (page congruence, no
+   overlap, entry/other fields unchanged, `p_filesz` within file), section and
+   dynamic byte identity (`.dynamic`, `.dynsym`, `.dynstr`, `.rela.*`, `.got*`,
+   `.plt*`), NX/GNU_STACK/RELRO, no W+X, no section/symbol/relocation in the
+   cave, no incoming branch or RIP-relative reference into the cave, all-zero
+   original filler, added-code register rules (no callee-saved writes, no `ret`,
+   no indirect transfer, single `sub rsp,8` alignment, `exit_group(1)` setup),
+   and a byte-diff/residue audit against the declared intervals.
+3. **Second parser view** — the bundle captures `readelf -lW` and the audit
+   cross-checks it field-by-field against the pyelftools view; missing `readelf`
+   is recorded as `not_run`, never assumed.
+4. **Reproducibility command** — `verify` builds twice and requires identical
+   bytes; the bundle embeds the result.
+5. **Evidence bundle** — one directory with original/candidate, manifest, audit,
+   reproducibility, environment fingerprint, independent views, a per-item
+   record, and a verifiable `SHA256SUMS`.
+6. **Contract revision** — a proposed frozen contract carrying the authorized
+   edits and the measured writer (see §3).
+
+---
+
+## 3. Contract revision (proposed; M5 confirms, Lead approves)
+
+File: `fixtures/public/CWE121_src_char_declare_cpy_51b/contract.route-a-v1.json`
+Reviewed-scope hash: `ba33b4d070b8799b778a9ca1a257190079627bda72b5c42933edfebb0f5d8fc4`
+
+The oracle constants are byte-identical to the frozen values (`dest=50`,
+`max_valid=49`, exit 1, empty stdout, 42-byte stderr). Only scope is extended:
+
+- six `authorized_edits`: exactly the amended handoff 09 §4.1 entries, including the
+  corrected `0x401309` resumption and the measured writer mechanism in entry 4;
+- `allowed_calls = ("fprintf", "printLine", "strcpy")` — `fprintf` is imported
+  in the ELF (`0x401120`) and `stderr` exists (`0x404080`); `fputs`/`fwrite`/
+  `write`/`exit` are **not** imported, so authorizing `fprintf` avoids a new
+  dependency and avoids an unmeasured seccomp-dependent syscall writer;
+- `environment_assumptions` record that the CET note is compile-time only and
+  that guest seccomp policy must be recorded.
+
+The file is **not** an approved contract until Member 5 (owner) confirms the
+writer amendment and the Lead approves. The probe contract
+(`contract.cave-probe.json`) remains a probe value, not the approved revision.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Evidence model — which artifact answers which Gate 3 item
+
+Handoff 11 §3 defines six required items. The bundle produces the static half;
+the guest run produces the runtime half.
+
+| # | Item | Produced by | In the bundle? |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | separate copy; original + manifests unchanged | bundle hashes; guest re-hash | yes (hashes) |
+| 2 | candidate identity, reproducibility, complete manifest | `edit-manifest.json`, `reproducibility.json` | yes |
+| 3 | structural audit: cave R-X, header extension, no overlap, flags/NX/RELRO/canary/W^X, readelf + ELF view, no relocation/import edit | `audit.json`, `readelf-*`, `objdump-*` | yes (static) |
+| 3b | cave mapped R-X at runtime, bytes match file, entry executes | gdb/runtime probe in guest | **no — guest step** |
+| 4 | six-case run, byte-exact, candidate hash before run, reverted snapshot | `routeb/run_manifest_repaired.py` under isolation | **no — guest step** |
+| 5 | isolation evidence for that run | snapshot revert, egress block, uid 1003 wrapper | **no — guest step** |
+| 6 | evidence bundle with hashes | `SHA256SUMS`, `bundle-sha256.txt` | yes |
+
+`gate3-record.md` is generated with items 4-5 explicitly `not_run`. It must not
+be upgraded to a gate pass from static evidence alone.
+
+---
+
+## 5. VM runbook (the only place these commands run)
+
+Prerequisites in the guest: repository at the design branch, Python 3.12,
+`pyelftools`, `capstone`, `binutils` (`readelf`, `objdump`); `lief` is not
+needed for the cave strategy. The candidate must be run only after the three
+isolation preconditions (clean snapshot, no egress, unprivileged user without
+passwordless sudo) hold.
+
+The static half (environment check, frozen hashes, tests, build, audit,
+reproducibility, bundle) is wrapped by `scripts/routea_vm_check.sh`. It is
+**unverified until the VM run** and deliberately stops before executing the
+candidate; the script prints the manual runtime steps.
+
+```bash
+CASE=fixtures/public/CWE121_src_char_declare_cpy_51b
+CONTRACT=$CASE/contract.route-a-v1.json
+
+# 0. tests (VM/CI only)
+python -m pytest tests/test_routea_cave.py tests/test_routea_manifest.py \
+  -q -p no:cacheprovider
+
+# 1. build, audit, reproducibility, static bundle
+python -m routea.cave bundle \
+  --elf $CASE/original.elf --contract $CONTRACT \
+  --cave 0x4018e9 --cave-size 1815 \
+  --out-dir var/jobs/m4-gate3/<run-id>/static --scope-authorized
+
+# 2. runtime cave probe (gdb, inside the isolation harness)
+#    - break at 0x401304 and 0x4018e9
+#    - `info proc mappings` must show r-xp covering 0x401000-0x401fff
+#    - memory at 0x4018e9 must equal the candidate file bytes
+#    - an instruction at the cave entry must decode and execute
+
+# 3. six frozen cases on the candidate, under the wrapper, from a reverted snapshot
+python routeb/run_manifest_repaired.py \
+  --binary <job>/candidate.elf --tests $CASE/tests \
+  --out var/jobs/m4-gate3/<run-id>/manifest-repaired.json
+
+# 4. original V0 shape for comparison (same session, documented 4/6)
+python routeb/run_manifest_repaired.py \
+  --binary $CASE/original.elf --tests $CASE/tests \
+  --out var/jobs/m4-gate3/<run-id>/manifest-original.json
+```
+
+Record for every run: candidate SHA-256 before and after, guest fingerprint, tool
+versions, wrapper attestation, snapshot revert log, and the raw stdout/stderr/rc
+of each case. Hashes and the per-item record are committed; large raw logs stay
+under `var/jobs/` and are cited by hash (handoff 12 §3).
+
+### Expected values
+
+| Check | Expected |
+|---|---|
+| candidate SHA-256 | `f3cb9cbb503fb0d47ebebab7053fa2ed37b7876ffe5122157d31fefc783f9fa7` |
+| contract hash | `ba33b4d070b8799b778a9ca1a257190079627bda72b5c42933edfebb0f5d8fc4` |
+| six cases | 4 valid: rc 0, stdout = input + LF; 2 invalid: rc 1, stdout empty, exactly 42-byte stderr; no crash |
+| original V0 | 4/6 (invalid cases fail by design: SIGSEGV on the original) |
+| mapping | `0x401000`-`0x401fff` mapped r-xp; cave bytes file-backed |
+
+A mismatch is a `FAIL`: report the case, the expected and actual bytes in hex, and
+the root cause. Never edit the oracle, the manifests, or the frozen hashes.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Test plan (not run on the host)
+
+| File | Needs ELF? | Run where | Covers |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `tests/test_routea_manifest.py` | no | anywhere | interval merge, residue, declared-interval audit, inclusive ranges |
+| `tests/test_routea_cave.py` | yes | guest/CI | plan bytes, manifest completeness, full audit, golden candidate hash, reproducibility, tamper rejection, readelf cross-view, CLI `verify`, CLI `bundle`, record item states |
+
+Golden hashes in the tests are drift detectors, not evidence: a mismatch means
+the design changed and must be re-reviewed. The suite is deliberately
+negative-first: an unpatched binary, an undeclared byte flip, and a tampered
+header must all fail the audit.
+
+**Host status:** `python -m py_compile` was run on every changed Python file.
+No ELF test, no `readelf`, no candidate execution was performed on the host. The
+suite must be run in the guest before any result is reported.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Open items
+
+1. **M5 confirms** the writer amendment in `contract.route-a-v1.json` and the
+   Lead approves the revision hash before the candidate freezes.
+2. **Guest run** produces items 3b, 4, 5 (runtime cave probe, six cases,
+   isolation evidence) under the M4 plan `12-m4-acceptance-evidence-plan.md`;
+   the plan's gdb breakpoints must use `0x401309`, not `0x401308`.
+3. **M3 isolation evidence** (deadline 2026-10-23 18:00) is a prerequisite for
+   item 4/5; missing isolation means `NOT VERIFIED`.
+4. **Independent replay** by M5 from the recorded commands before the Lead
+   approves the Gate 3 label.
+5. Fixture freeze stays blocked until gates 3-5 evidence exists; no new freeze
+   date is promised here.
